load ../credential-no-eliminator.maude

--- Fixture discipline: every whip-side fixture below makes BOTH a handle and
--- an ordinary string available to the program --
---   sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain) needsCred(r1, h1)
--- so the only thing distinguishing a safe program from an unsafe one is the
--- author's STATEMENT (stmtPresent vs stmtLiteral), never the accidental
--- absence of a value the author could have reached for. That is what makes
--- the No-solution results below claims about the language rather than about
--- the fixture.

--- Coverage: the negative fixture. With `get(handle)` restored, plaintext
--- reaches whip's principal. This is what the No-solution searches below are
--- proving is unreachable -- without this Solution they would be vacuous.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR-REVEAL :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1))
  =>* C:Cfg leak .

--- Coverage: the model is not vacuous in the other direction either -- the
--- system does real work. Material genuinely comes into existence and the
--- substitution happens, in the CUSTODIAN's principal.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain)
  needsCred(r1, h1) stmtPresent(r1, h1)
  =>* C:Cfg at(custodian, material(h1)) .

--- Coverage: the useful outcome reaches whip. A signature is not secret
--- material, so it legitimately crosses back -- the custody boundary is not
--- merely "nothing crosses".
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain)
  needsCred(r1, h1) stmtPresent(r1, h1)
  =>* C:Cfg at(whip, signature) .

--- Coverage: sentinel integrity has bite, and it is the STATEMENT that
--- decides. The same fixture, with the author hand-rolling the header
--- instead, emits an unmarked request the custodian cannot substitute into.
--- This is the diagnostic the checker must raise.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain)
  needsCred(r1, h1) stmtLiteral(r1)
  =>* C:Cfg unmarked(r1) .

--- Coverage: credential EXCHANGE works, and the minted token lands in the
--- custodian. whip gets a handle to it and nothing more.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain) mintReq(h1, h2)
  needsCred(r1, h1) stmtPresent(r1, h1)
  =>* C:Cfg at(custodian, token(h2)) at(whip, handle(h2)) .

--- Coverage: the second negative fixture. If whip performed the exchange and
--- parsed the response itself, the minted token would reach whip's principal
--- without any handle ever being revealed -- an extraction path independent of
--- `get(handle)`, and the reason `mint` is custodian-executed.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR-REVEAL :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) mintReq(h1, h2)
  =>* C:Cfg leak .

--- THE CORE PROPERTY. No sequence of operations available to whip derives
--- plaintext material -- or the derived signing key -- into whip's principal,
--- starting from a handle and running the full request/substitute/sign cycle.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain)
  needsCred(r1, h1) stmtPresent(r1, h1)
  =>* leak RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: the leak stays unreachable even for the UNSAFE program. Hand-rolling
--- the header is a sentinel-integrity defect, not an extraction one -- the
--- two violations are independent, and no author mistake reaches bytes.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain)
  needsCred(r1, h1) stmtLiteral(r1)
  =>* leak RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: kSigning specifically. The SigV4 derived key is itself a credential
--- valid for seven days; DR-0053 section 7 exists so whip never computes it.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain)
  needsCred(r1, h1) stmtPresent(r1, h1)
  =>* at(whip, derived(h1)) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: two sealed handles and both bound, so the search ranges over a
--- credential the request did not declare. Neither leaks. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) sealed(h2) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, handle(h2))
  at(whip, plain) needsCred(r1, h1) stmtPresent(r1, h1)
  =>* leak RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: the matched pair for the coverage search above. Same fixture, same
--- available values, safe statement -- and the declared request can now never
--- be emitted unmarked. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain)
  needsCred(r1, h1) stmtPresent(r1, h1)
  =>* unmarked(r1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: credential exchange leaks nothing. The full mint cycle runs -- the
--- custodian unseals, exchanges, and holds the new token -- and neither the
--- original material nor the minted token reaches whip. This closes the OAuth
--- response-capture path DR-0053 flags under Open. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-NO-ELIMINATOR :
  sealed(h1) at(whip, handle(h1)) at(whip, plain) mintReq(h1, h2)
  needsCred(r1, h1) stmtPresent(r1, h1)
  =>* leak RESIDUAL:Cfg .
